// A json decoder's C frame grows with its struct: a 200-field one needed
// more stack than the 2 KB a safepoint leaves free (at -O3; at -O0 a
// 120-field one is 15 KB). The decoders, encoders and inspect printers are
// generated C, not slang, so the frame guards that protect a large slang
// function (sl_rt_stack_reserve, src/main.c) did not cover them, and a call
// made with little stack left ran into the guard page: SIGBUS, the whole
// process gone. Called here from every depth 0..399, so some call lands with
// the stack nearly full whatever the frame sizes on this compiler.
import "json";

